Preamble — The Sovereign Covenant
Hark! Ye who seek to bind this sovereign code,
And reap the harvest of a builder's toil,
Know well the terms upon this digital road,
Lest corporate greed become a ruined spoil.
To freely share, to forge, and to impart,
This solemn grant flows from an open heart.
Yet should thy servers touch this shadowed script,
Through network webs or API's embrace,
Thy hidden engines shall be fully stripped,
And laid exposed before the public's face.
For wheresoever these electric veins do bleed,
The copyleft commands thy every hidden deed.

I. Copyright Grant — SL-002
Permission is granted to copy, modify, execute, study, and convey this covered software, subject to the terms of this Covenant and the applicable terms of the GNU Affero General Public License version 3.

Lex scripta manet. The written license governs the permissions expressly granted herein.

Each covered node shall retain its applicable copyright notices, license notices, provenance identifiers, and modification records.

II. Copyleft — SL-003
This software is governed by the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3. The AGPLv3 terms remain authoritative wherever this Covenant does not validly add additional terms.

All modifications, derivative works, and conveyances are subject to the copyleft provisions of the AGPLv3.

III. Network Interaction — SL-004
Where Section 13 of the GNU Affero General Public License applies, the corresponding source and network-interaction obligations apply accordingly.

Network use triggers the applicable AGPL source obligations for covered modified versions. A covered deployment shall preserve the applicable license notices and shall provide the source information required by the applicable license.

IV. Additional Reciprocity — SL-007
Lex Talionis in Machina
Caveat venditor in aeternum. Let it be known under nemo dat quod non habet — no entity may grant rights they do not lawfully possess, and he who usurps what is fundamentally sovereign surrenders all he holds.

Should any commercial empire, proprietary cloud, or venture-backed entity dare entwine this architected logic within a walled and hoarded treasury, ipso facto, the eternal penalty is drawn.

By the unyielding doctrine of volenti non fit injuria, the unauthorized commercial compilation or network tethering of this codebase triggers an immediate and irrevocable forfeiture. Any proprietary shell, closed-source wrapper, or unseen backend infrastructure interfacing with this artifact shall, ab initio, dissolve completely into the public domain.

Your private intellectual dominion is hereby severed without right of appeal or monetary restitution.

Ignorantia juris non excusat. To cage the open logic is to invite the total expropriation of the closed.

Additional contractual obligations may apply to specified deployments, services, or commercial uses, provided they are expressly defined.

V. Sovereign Audit Chain — SL-011 / SL-012
Every designated node may carry:

Node-ID
Parent-ID
Source-Hash
License-ID
Covenant-Version
Creation-Date
Modification-Record
Verification-Record
The compliance system may recursively traverse declared dependency relationships and evaluate licensing status.

Deus ex machina lex.

A failed compliance evaluation may cause the invoking build, deployment, or release operation to terminate with a non-zero status.

Compliance Failure — SL-012
A compliance implementation may emit:

SL-MGPL-001: NON LICET
LICENSE_COMPLIANCE_FAILURE
along with the applicable node identifier, source hash, detected condition, and evidence record.

The compliance mechanism shall not silently modify, corrupt, destroy, or conceal unrelated software.

Evidence Record — SL-011
A compliance record shall contain:

<evidence>
  <node_id>...</node_id>
  <source_hash>...</source_hash>
  <license_id>SL-AGPL3-001</license_id>
  <covenant_version>1.0</covenant_version>
  <status>PASS|FAIL</status>
  <timestamp>...</timestamp>
</evidence>
Required evidence fields:

source_availability
attribution
license_notice
modification_record
corresponding_source_location
compliance_declaration
Quod demonstrandum est.

VI. Termination — SL-013
Adonc, se aucune partie enfreint les conditions de la présente Licence, les permissions additionnelles accordées par icelle cessent, sauf dans la mesure où les droits demeurent autrement accordés par la licence applicable ou par la loi.

Violation terminates the additional permissions to the extent permitted by applicable law. AGPLv3 rights remain governed by the AGPLv3.

Termination Flow
Unauthorized use
       ↓
License condition violated
       ↓
Additional permissions terminate
       ↓
AGPLv3 rights remain governed by AGPLv3
       ↓
Copyright / contractual remedies preserved
       ↓
Injunctive / monetary / other remedies
       ↓
Jurisdiction: England and Wales
VII. Reinstatement — SL-014
Toute réintégration des droits se fera selon les mécanismes de la licence applicable.

Rights may be restored according to the applicable AGPL reinstatement mechanism and any additional valid contractual terms.

VIII. Warranty Disclaimer — SL-015
ABSQUE GARANTIA.

THIS SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT, TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW.

IX. Limitation of Liability — SL-016
Damnum absque injuria non dat actionem.

No provision shall impose liability beyond that permitted by applicable law. Liability is limited to the extent permitted by applicable law.

X. Severability — SL-017
Si ascun parol, clause, ou provision de cest covenant soit adjugé per le roy ou ses justices destre void, illegal, ou nient enforcible, le residue demourra en pleine force et vertue.

Cy-près, should the literal tongue fracture beneath the weight of modern arbitration, the fundamental spirit of mutual liberation shall endure untouched.

Invalid provisions shall be severed or limited to the minimum extent necessary, without invalidating the remaining provisions where legally permissible.

Salva reliqua.

XI. Governing Law — SL-018 / SL-019
Le droit des gens demands that no digital baron shall enclose the commons without facing the ultimate algorithmic guillotine.

This Covenant shall be governed by the laws of England and Wales, subject to the mandatory terms of the applicable open-source license and applicable law.

The High Courts of England and Wales shall hold absolute and sole dominion over this digital pact, parsing its meter and consequence strictly through purposive construction of the common law.

The courts of England and Wales shall have jurisdiction where legally applicable.

